--TEST--
a path argument that starts with a relative path given as a string literal and adds a value built while the program runs is relative on every run, so it does not compile and the help names `Core\Path::thisDir` — `rule:programs/relative-paths-resolve-from-their-file`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The string literal is joined to nothing: the whole path is built while the program runs.
string $name = 'note';
echo Core\IO::read('data/' . $name . '.txt');
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0840]: this path is relative when the program runs, so the call always throws an error
  --> case.nvs:4:20
  |
4 | echo Core\IO::read('data/' . $name . '.txt');
  |                    ^^^^^^^ a relative path, with more added while the program runs
  = help: start the path with the folder of this file: `Core\Path::thisDir('data') . '/' . $name`, or `Core\Path::join(Core\Path::thisDir('data'), $name)`

error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
